course: dictionary
lesson: 1554
title: Many meanings of chance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chance is a word with several meanings. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Saying calmly and privately "I don't like it when you do that in front of them" gives a real friend the chance to stop.» Here a chance is an opportunity, a time when you can do something. The friend can stop, so the sentence is about a good moment to act.
explain: Chance can also mean how likely something is. In maths, an event that has an even chance is just as likely to happen as not. Tossing a coin gives an even chance of heads, which people also call fifty-fifty. A die has six sides, so rolling a 6 has a 1 in 6 chance.
explain: Chance can mean luck, things that happen without anyone planning them. «In a game of chance nobody is to blame for losing» means that the result came from luck, not from anyone's mistake. Chess is a game of thinking, so it is not a game of chance.
explain: Some phrases use chance in special ways. «Don't take chances» means don't take risks. «Give someone a second chance» means forgive them. «Chance it» is informal and means try something risky and hope it works. Use the context to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A chance can be an opportunity, a time when you are able to do something.
fact: Chance can also mean how likely something is to happen, on a scale from impossible to certain.
fact: An even chance is fifty-fifty: both results are equally likely.
fact: Chance can mean luck, when things happen without anyone planning them.
fact: «By chance» means without planning, and «a fair chance» means a reasonable opportunity.
exercise: «Saying calmly and privately "I don't like it when you do that" gives a real friend the chance to stop.» What does chance mean here? | A 1 in 6 risk | *An opportunity to do something | A loud argument | Luck, with nobody planning it
exercise: What is the chance of rolling a 6 on a die? | *1 in 6 | Certain | 1 in 2 | Impossible
exercise: «Don't take chances» on a icy path means what? | Make a list of the path | *Don't take risks | Always win the race | Take as many risks as you can
exercise: «In a game of chance nobody is to blame for losing.» Which meaning of chance fits? | How likely something is to happen | *Luck, things happening without anyone planning them | An opportunity to try again | A way of being forgiven
test: A coin toss has an even chance of heads. What does even chance mean? | Only one way it can go | *Fifty-fifty, equally likely | Certain, sure to happen | Impossible, never going to happen
test: Otter watches there «on the chance, you know, just on the chance!» What does on the chance mean? | By mistake | Without thinking at all | Very quickly | *Just in case
exam: In «David had a chance to help his friend», the word chance means: | How likely something is to happen | Luck, things happening without planning | *An opportunity to do something | To try something risky and hope it works
